  },
  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Proverbs",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 10,
    "summary": "A wise son makes a glad father—The mouth of a righteous man is a well of life—He who utters slander is a fool—The desire of the righteous will be granted.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "The proverbs of Solomon. A wise son maketh a glad father: but a foolish son is the heaviness of his mother.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 12,
            "text": "1 Kgs. 4:32; Prov. 1:1; 25:1."
          },
          {
            "start": 27,
            "end": 31,
            "text": "Prov. 17:21."
          },
          {
            "start": 45,
            "end": 49,
            "text": "TG Happiness."
          },
          {
            "start": 50,
            "end": 56,
            "text": "TG Marriage, Fatherhood."
          },
          {
            "start": 64,
            "end": 71,
            "text": "Prov. 15:5, 20."
          },
          {
            "start": 83,
            "end": 92,
            "text": "OR sorrow."
          },
          {
            "start": 100,
            "end": 106,
            "text": "TG Family, Children, Duties of; Marriage, Motherhood."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 76,
            "end": 78
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Treasures of wickedness profit nothing: but righteousness delivereth from death.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 9,
            "text": "TG Treasure."
          },
          {
            "start": 44,
            "end": 57,
            "text": "TG Righteousness."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The Lord will not suffer the soul of the righteous to famish: but he casteth away the substance of the wicked.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "He becometh poor that dealeth with a slack hand: but the hand of the diligent maketh rich.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 37,
            "end": 42,
            "text": "TG Laziness."
          },
          {
            "start": 69,
            "end": 77,
            "text": "TG Dedication; Diligence."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 30,
            "end": 34
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "He that gathereth in summer is a wise son: but he that sleepeth in harvest is a son that causeth shame.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 28,
            "end": 30
          },
          {
            "start": 43,
            "end": 46
          },
          {
            "start": 75,
            "end": 77
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Blessings are upon the head of the just: but violence covereth the mouth of the wicked.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 9,
            "text": "D&C 39:8."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 10,
            "end": 13
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The memory of the just is blessed: but the name of the wicked shall rot.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 55,
            "end": 61,
            "text": "TG Wickedness."
          },
          {
            "start": 68,
            "end": 71,
            "text": "Isa. 14:22; Jer. 51:62 (61–62)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 23,
            "end": 25
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The wise in heart will receive commandments: but a prating fool shall fall.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "He that walketh uprightly walketh surely: but he that perverteth his ways shall be known.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 15,
            "text": "TG Walking with God."
          },
          {
            "start": 16,
            "end": 25,
            "text": "Prov. 28:6."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "He that winketh with the eye causeth sorrow: but a prating fool shall fall.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The mouth of a righteous man is a well of life: but violence covereth the mouth of the wicked.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 15,
            "end": 24,
            "text": "Ps. 37:30; Alma 36:26; D&C 108:7."
          },
          {
            "start": 34,
            "end": 38,
            "text": "Prov. 13:14."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 25,
            "end": 31
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Hatred stirreth up strifes: but love covereth all sins.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 6,
            "text": "TG Hate; Malice."
          },
          {
            "start": 19,
            "end": 26,
            "text": "TG Contention."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "In the lips of him that hath understanding wisdom is found: but a rod is for the back of him that is void of understanding.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 66,
            "end": 69,
            "text": "Prov. 19:29."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 70,
            "end": 72
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Wise men lay up knowledge: but the mouth of the foolish is near destruction.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 35,
            "end": 40,
            "text": "Prov. 18:7."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 5,
            "end": 8
          },
          {
            "start": 56,
            "end": 58
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The rich man’s wealth is his strong city: the destruction of the poor is their poverty.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 15,
            "end": 21,
            "text": "Prov. 18:11."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 22,
            "end": 24
          },
          {
            "start": 70,
            "end": 72
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The labour of the righteous tendeth to life: the fruit of the wicked to sin.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 10,
            "text": "TG Labor; Work, Value of."
          },
          {
            "start": 39,
            "end": 43,
            "text": "Prov. 19:23."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 28,
            "end": 35
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "He is in the way of life that keepeth instruction: but he that refuseth reproof erreth.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 38,
            "end": 49,
            "text": "TG Teachable."
          },
          {
            "start": 72,
            "end": 79,
            "text": "TG Chastening; Reproof."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 3,
            "end": 8
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "He that hideth hatred with lying lips, and he that uttereth a slander, is a fool.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 15,
            "end": 21,
            "text": "TG Hate."
          },
          {
            "start": 62,
            "end": 69,
            "text": "TG Slander."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 22,
            "end": 26
          },
          {
            "start": 71,
            "end": 73
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "In the multitude of words there wanteth not sin: but he that refraineth his lips is wise.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 20,
            "end": 25,
            "text": "TG Boast."
          },
          {
            "start": 61,
            "end": 71,
            "text": "Prov. 17:27."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 81,
            "end": 83
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The tongue of the just is as choice silver: the heart of the wicked is little worth.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 23,
            "end": 28
          },
          {
            "start": 68,
            "end": 70
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The lips of the righteous feed many: but fools die for want of wisdom.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 41,
            "end": 46,
            "text": "Ps. 14:1 (1–7)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The blessing of the Lord, it maketh rich, and he addeth no sorrow with it.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 36,
            "end": 40,
            "text": "TG Treasure."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "It is as sport to a fool to do mischief: but a man of understanding hath wisdom.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 5
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The fear of the wicked, it shall come upon him: but the desire of the righteous shall be granted.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "As the whirlwind passeth, so is the wicked no more: but the righteous is an everlasting foundation.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 29,
            "end": 31
          },
          {
            "start": 46,
            "end": 51
          },
          {
            "start": 70,
            "end": 72
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "As vinegar to the teeth, and as smoke to the eyes, so is the sluggard to them that send him.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 54,
            "end": 56
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The fear of the Lord prolongeth days: but the years of the wicked shall be shortened.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 8,
            "text": "TG Reverence."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The hope of the righteous shall be gladness: but the expectation of the wicked shall perish.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 8,
            "text": "TG Hope."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 26,
            "end": 34
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The way of the Lord is strength to the upright: but destruction shall be to the workers of iniquity.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 23,
            "end": 31,
            "text": "TG Strength."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 20,
            "end": 22
          },
          {
            "start": 64,
            "end": 72
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The righteous shall never be removed: but the wicked shall not inhabit the earth.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 13,
            "text": "Prov. 2:21 (21–22)."
          },
          {
            "start": 29,
            "end": 36,
            "text": "Lam. 1:8."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The mouth of the just bringeth forth wisdom: but the froward tongue shall be cut out.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 53,
            "end": 60,
            "text": "OR perverse."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The lips of the righteous know what is acceptable: but the mouth of the wicked speaketh frowardness.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 59,
            "end": 64,
            "text": "Eccl. 10:12."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 79,
            "end": 87
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      }
    ]
  },
